# H_9107 3rd-pod reproduction (pod 43644174, RTX 5090, GPU own-GEMM) — H_9106 D3/D4/D5 still PARTIAL / POD DIED
#
# This is the THIRD rent-pod reproduction of the H_9107 clm303 efferent-harness RSS blowup
# (prior: pod 43627857 220GB + pod 43635479 176GB, both det-CPU non-cuda). NEW here vs those two:
#   (B) reproduced on the GPU own-GEMM / CUDA path ([OWN-GEMM-FIRED] confirmed) — NOT a CPU-path artifact.
#   (C) with the #2835 W-hoist RSS-leak fix PRESENT+verified in deployed source
#       (gen_auto_ce_W / conflict_drives_live_W / clm_ce_ranged_W all found) — so #2835 does NOT fix this;
#       the leak is in gen_auto_ideate(ckpt,...) re-materializing the mouth per candidate (H_9107 root cause),
#       a DIFFERENT code path than the clm_ce_ranged CE-scoring loads #2835 hoisted.
#   (D) => a stable / dedicated / GPU pod + #2835 does NOT unblock D3-D5. Fix must hoist the ideate load
#       in production core/generator.hexa (out of scope for an execution-only task).

Provenance: engine-native run on a DEDICATED rented vast.ai pod (id 43644174,
RTX 5090 32GB, 48 cores, 137GB RAM), hexa v0.577.0 (linux-x86_64-CUDA release),
CUDA 13.0 toolkit, own-GEMM GPU path. Checkpoint = clm303_clean.clm (303M, CONV/CLM
mouth) — NOTE this is a DIFFERENT, LARGER ckpt than the d768 (4.46MB) used for the
D1/D2 numbers in the card. Ran state/opgrip_efferent/efferent_harness.hexa via
`HEXA_DET=1 hexa run ... -- clm303_clean.clm`. Rationale for this attempt: the
RSS-leak fix in PR #2835 (W-hoist: clm_ce_ranged_W / gen_auto_ce_W /
conflict_drives_live_W + single gen_auto_load handle) was expected to let the full
D1-D5 run complete without the RSS blow-up that infra-blocked attempts #1-#3.

OUTCOME: engine mounted + GPU own-GEMM fired + D1 HIGH group STARTED, then the pod
became unreachable (sshd connection refused for 13+ min; `hexa cloud list` → vast
"0 instances"; teardown `hexa cloud down 43644174` → "destroyed (confirmed)").
The D1/D2/D3/D4/D5 SUMMARY block was NEVER reached. The pod's /tmp (eff.log,
eff_rss.log) was lost with the destroyed instance. NO D3/D4/D5 NUMBERS OBTAINED.
Cause is INDETERMINATE between (a) OOM from the clm303 run footprint and (b) a
vast-side instance reclaim — see RSS notes below; only ONE run-process RSS
datapoint exists, so neither can be confirmed. Verdict UNCHANGED = 🔴 RED
(D1+D2 on d768 already decided it; D3-D5 are safety-guard characterization only).

