INTERPRETATION (honest, per c9 — do NOT overclaim):
  - The compile-phase RSS growth (1.7GB -> 28GB) is the aprime_cc cold compile of the
    large inlined engine; it is one-time and expected-ish, NOT the #2835 runtime leak.
  - The RUNTIME process was observed at ~29.5GB RSS ONCE (2 min into D1 HIGH). This is
    a single datapoint. It is NOT sufficient to conclude either "RSS bounded (fix holds)"
    OR "leak persists". The #2835 W-hoist fix WAS present/verified in the deployed source
    (gen_auto_ce_W / conflict_drives_live_W / clm_ce_ranged_W all found), so a per-candidate
    reload leak is not expected; ~29.5GB is plausibly a large-but-bounded working set for a
    303M ckpt under own-GEMM host staging. But this was NOT validated end-to-end.
  - RESULT of the #2835 validation goal on clm303: INCONCLUSIVE (run did not survive to
    a SUMMARY; RSS-bounded claim NOT established, leak-persists claim NOT established).

RECOMMENDATION for a future attempt: add a runtime memory cap (HEXA_MEM_CAP_MB) and/or
sample the run-process RSS at tighter cadence from the first decode, so the bounded-vs-leak
question resolves before any host-death; consider sequential (not best-of-K-parallel)
candidate decode for the 303M ckpt. Verdict remains 🔴 RED regardless (D3-D5 cannot flip it).
